<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anton Lutskevich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Anton Luckievič</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anton Lutskevich was a Belarusian politician and publicist, a founder of the Belarusian national movement. He led the government of the Belarusian People's Republic from 1918 to 1920 and sought international recognition for it. He later worked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Wilno</a> under Polish rule and died after arrest by the Soviet authorities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anton-lutskevich.jpg" alt="Anton Lutskevich" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anton_Luckievi%C4%8D,_kartka.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
